9:["$","div",null,{"className":"text-content-secondary text-center italic","children":"By Asari AI"}]
a:["$","p",null,{"children":"Our mission is to empower people to co-invent the future with AI agents. This is a grand challenge: agents must reason consistently over long horizons, manage complex architectural tradeoffs, and meet rigorous verification standards. These skills are crucial when inventing new systems that go beyond the training data of today’s AI models."}]
b:["$","div",null,{"style":{"width":"100%","margin":"0.5rem 0","textAlign":"center"},"children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/asari-website-proposal/original-asari/assets/blog-visuals/code_comparison.svg","alt":"Code comparison between C and Rust implementations","style":{"maxWidth":"100%","height":"auto"}}]}]
c:["$","div",null,{"className":"text-content-secondary font-family-sans text-center","style":{"fontSize":"0.75rem","marginTop":"0.25rem"},"children":["$","p",null,{"children":"Translating C to Rust involves both direct line-by-line conversions and\nlanguage-specific reimplementations. Color coding shows which code segments\ntranslate directly versus require Rust-specific idioms, with test coverage\nindicators showing equivalent and unique validation approaches."}]}]
d:["$","p",null,{"children":["As a foundational step, we've applied our AI agents to translating critical software systems from C to ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/nomicon/meet-safe-and-unsafe.html","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"external-link-in-content","children":"Safe Rust"}],". This provides an ideal proving ground for developing agents that reliably complete long-horizon tasks while addressing serious security concerns."]}]
e:["$","p",null,{"children":"The result? The Rust implementations are memory safe, performant, and adhere to the meticulous testing standards necessary for essential infrastructure. For code designed to run on spacecraft, our agents produced a version that actually surpasses the original C version in accuracy."}]
f:["$","div",null,{"className":"border-2 border-brand-tertiary/70 rounded-lg p-6 my-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"text-brand-primary font-semibold mb-3 flex items-center gap-2","style":{"fontFamily":"'Didact Gothic', 'Inter', 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif"},"children":[["$","$L51",null,{"size":20,"color":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Code that flies"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"text-brand-primary/80 text-sm","style":{"fontFamily":"'Didact Gothic', 'Inter', 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif"},"children":[["$","p",null,{"children":["For ",["$","code",null,{"children":"libmcs"}],", code designed to run in space, our agents not only produced a Rust translation passing all ESA-standard tests, but also improved the test suite itself by finding subtle errors expert reviewers had missed."]}],["$","blockquote",null,{"className":"border-l-4 border-brand-tertiary pl-4 mt-4 mb-0 text-brand-primary/70 italic","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"“Asari AI were able to find a very subtle double error in our test suite which we never spotted throughout years of reviews.”"}],["$","footer",null,{"className":"text-brand-tertiary text-xs mt-2 not-italic","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"— GTD-GmbH, European Space Agency (ESA) flight software verifier"}]}]]}]]}]]}]
10:["$","h2",null,{"id":"the-need-for-safe-software-infrastructure","children":"The need for safe software infrastructure"}]
11:["$","p",null,{"children":["C code powers critical infrastructure systems worldwide, but its lack of memory safety creates vulnerabilities that account for 70% of serious security bugs in ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://media.defense.gov/2022/Nov/10/2003112742/-1/-1/0/CSI_SOFTWARE_MEMORY_SAFETY.PDF","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"external-link-in-content","children":"major codebases"}],". Rust eliminates these vulnerabilities by design through its ownership system and compile-time ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memory_safety","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"external-link-in-content","children":"memory safety"}]," checks."]}]
12:["$","p",null,{"children":["Translating billions of lines of C to memory-safe Rust is a national security imperative, as outlined in the DARPA's Translate all C to Rust (",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://www.darpa.mil/research/programs/translating-all-c-to-rust","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"external-link-in-content","children":"TRACTOR"}],") program. Completing this task requires understanding system architecture, redesigning for different memory models, and verifying correctness across complex codebases. This is exactly the kind of intricate work that demands dependable collaboration between humans and AI agents."]}]
13:["$","p",null,{"children":["One of the key capabilities of our agents is reliably completing long-horizon projects with rigorous testing standards. We challenged our agents with ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"migrating four widely-used production C libraries to Safe Rust"}],". These four libraries are part of the TRACTOR initiative and collectively total 40K+ lines of low-level systems, performance-critical code:"]}]
14:["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"libmcs"}]}]," (Mathematical library for Critical Systems): high-precision math library that meets strict European Space Agency (ESA) standards"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"gzip"}]}],": one of the most widely-used command-line tools for file compression"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"libyaml"}]}],": the foundational parsing library used for YAML configuration files"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"zlib"}]}],": compression library used by virtually every operating system and application for data compression"]}],"\n"]}]
15:["$","p",null,{"children":["We are releasing the translated Rust libraries ",["$","a",null,{"href":"#open-source-safe-rust-translations","target":"$undefined","rel":"$undefined","className":"$undefined","children":"here"}],", and are excited to hear what you think!"]}]
16:["$","h2",null,{"id":"the-challenges-of-system-design","children":"The challenges of system design"}]
17:["$","p",null,{"children":"Migrating C code to Safe Rust can appear deceptively straightforward: take C code as input, produce equivalent code in Rust as output. But what does equivalent actually mean? C and Rust rely on fundamentally different principles, with no direct line-for-line mapping between code in the two languages."}]
