a3:["$","p",null,{"children":"This algorithm is preferred in libm because it guarantees correct rounding for the last bit. Newton-Raphson converges very quickly, but it can suffer from “off-by-one-ULP” (Unit in the Last Place) errors unless calculated with significantly higher precision than the target type. This bit-by-bit method is slower, but mathematically rigorous for integer-based floating point units."}]
